WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.334
Software architecture helps us reason about a system
that is too complex to hold entirely in our

00:00:06.334 --> 00:00:06.730
heads.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:10.557
The slides use growing codebases to motivate this
problem.

00:00:10.557 --> 00:00:16.693
Architecture connects requirements to important
structural decisions, and helps people locate

00:00:16.693 --> 00:00:19.663
changes, examine quality, and plan evolution.

00:00:19.663 --> 00:00:22.962
Size alone does not determine the effort required.

00:00:22.962 --> 00:00:29.296
Ask which decisions affect many parts of the system,
and which assumptions would be expensive to

00:00:29.296 --> 00:00:29.758
change.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.422
Begin with the system mission, its environment, and
its stakeholders.

00:00:34.422 --> 00:00:39.178
Then identify the decisions that strongly shape
structure and behavior.

00:00:39.178 --> 00:00:45.340
Architecture includes important responsibilities,
interfaces, relationships, and principles.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:48.220
Not every design choice has the same reach.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:53.579
Even an algorithm can be architectural when it
determines a system-wide quality.

00:00:53.579 --> 00:00:59.875
The purpose is to support communication and
analysis, so a useful description explains why its

00:00:59.875 --> 00:01:02.555
decisions matter to the people involved.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:06.773
An intended architecture states how a system should
be organized.

00:01:06.773 --> 00:01:09.983
An implemented architecture describes what exists.

00:01:09.983 --> 00:01:16.340
Drift adds undocumented decisions without violating
the intended design; erosion breaks an intended

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:17.046
constraint.

00:01:17.046 --> 00:01:23.274
To distinguish them, first identify the actual rule,
then inspect evidence of the implementation.

00:01:23.274 --> 00:01:26.741
Architecture recovery helps reconstruct that
evidence.

00:01:26.741 --> 00:01:33.097
A team can repair a violation or consciously revise
a decision, but should keep its description and

00:01:33.097 --> 00:01:35.280
rationale aligned with the result.
